<p>President Trump ended a two-day summit with Chinese President Xi Jinping in Beijing after saying the United States and China had reached “fantastic trade deals” and “settled a lot of different problems,” but the trip produced few public details on agreements beyond broad trade and cooperation statements. Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi said the sides agreed to continue implementing previous trade agreements and establish trade and investment councils, while Xi said they had reached common understandings on stable economic and trade ties, practical cooperation and each side’s concerns. Trump said he and Xi discussed Taiwan at length, including U.S. arms sales, despite earlier White House assurances that Taiwan would not be on the summit agenda. He said he made “no commitment either way” to Xi and would decide soon on a $14 billion weapons package for Taiwan, which Congress approved in January but has not moved forward. Taiwan urged Washington to proceed with arms sales, calling them central to regional peace and its defense. Boeing confirmed that China had committed to buying 200 aircraft, reopening a Chinese order pipeline after years without a major Boeing sale, though the order was smaller than some investors had expected. Trump also said he and Xi discussed possible guardrails for artificial intelligence and a potential U.S.-Russia-China nuclear arms pact. On Iran and the Strait of Hormuz, reports described Chinese statements as limited or noncommittal beyond general calls for stability.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/VzLXJ9ln-lkID3TdnDlGD1WDsMt32NX3S2T0QNVgS-mtFMhhxdiuJQvC-luIaDPU_L-oGxGh3apxfYsjLHEiJ7B9zn4Vg0m0N1ChAI87Pa8BatRanRPDMlnUf6tcRSj_KefrXJIxdgTP_gD3gfAaUaGyaCW8vTnrrt8eexA-Zri8437pgy--t2fkNfZ37Knwao65xGQh2I4-pO2hjCWg9BKCKgoD8PP_sOzdNJhIra3u8qO_2Zcno7GZWhjA1svhYdmKr7Dm64IZTtidlw' alt='US President Donald Trump boards Air Force One before his departure from Beijing Capital Airport.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Taiwan policy: Trump said Xi opposed Taiwan independence and asked whether the United States would defend the island if China attacked, but Trump said he declined to answer and maintained ambiguity.</li><li>Tariffs: The Straits Times noted that, despite trade being central to expectations for the summit, the word “tariff” was not mentioned in the public takeaways it examined.</li><li>Summit format: SCMP reported that the final day did not include the kind of deal-signing ceremony attended by leaders that has often accompanied state visits to China.</li><li>Future meetings: Chinese officials said Xi would travel to the United States later in 2026 at Trump’s invitation, according to reports on the post-summit readout.</li></ul><blockquote>I’ll make a determination over the next fairly short period - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump described Xi as a “great leader” and “friend” and said he wanted “sincere and deep” communication with him. (<a href='https://gnnhd.tv/news/55174/trump-concludes-visit-to-china-says-made-fantastic-trade-deals-with-xi'>GNN</a>, <a href='https://www.teletica.com/internacional/trump-y-xi-jinping-ponen-fin-a-historico-encuentro-en-pekin_408817'>Teletica</a>)</li><li>Chinese government and analysts: Beijing’s post-summit statements emphasized Xi’s phrase “constructive strategic stability” and included few public deal announcements. (<a href='https://www.asianews.it/news-en/Trump-and-Xi-in-Beijing%3A-suggestive-words-and-images%2C-but-few-deals-65452.html'>AsiaNews</a>)</li><li>Taiwan: Taiwanese national-security officials read Trump’s post-summit comments as signaling no change in U.S. policy, with the status quo remaining the key point. (<a href='https://www.ettoday.net/news/20260516/3166940.htm'>ETtoday</a>)</li><li>U.S. lawmakers: Members of Congress pushed Trump to maintain military support for Taiwan after he left the proposed weapons package unresolved. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/lawmakers-press-trump-for-military-support-for-taiwan-after-he-leaves-arms-package-unresolved/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Boeing: Boeing said the agreement was a first tranche, expected more commitments and declined to specify which aircraft models were being discussed. (<a href='https://www.cna.com.tw/news/aopl/202605160015.aspx'>CNA</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/05/15/big-promises-thin-results-from-trumps-china-trip-00924309'>Big promises, thin results from Trump’s China trip</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/trump-and-xi-pledge-strategic-stability-but-key-questions-remain-unanswered'>Trump and Xi pledge &#x27;strategic stability&#x27; but key questions remain unanswered</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/why-were-there-no-splashy-deals-at-the-trump-xi-summit'>Why were there no splashy deals at the Trump-Xi summit?</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-concludes-china-visit-hailing-fantastic-deals/article70983165.ece'>Trump says U.S., China ‘settled a lot of problems’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/05/16/trump-closes-china-visit-without-substantial-agreements-but-with-xi-s-offer-on-strait-of-hormuz'>Trump closes China visit without substantial agreements but with Xi&#x27;s offer on Strait of Hormuz</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Asia-Pacific/2026/0515/Trump-Xi-Beijing-summit-US-China'>Beyond the pomp and pageantry, Xi Jinping sent a message to Donald Trump</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/why-china-didnt-hand-trump-breakthrough-iran'>Why China didn’t hand Trump a breakthrough on Iran</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/donald-trump-2-day-china-visit-live-updates-donald-trump-beijing-xi-jinping-bilateral-meeting-iran-war-trade-tariff-boeing-taiwan-1